-- title:
--   Adelic index quotient is K-linearly isomorphic to H¹(D)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying `HasPrincipalDivisors K F`, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a finitely supported divisor $D$ with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v(f)$ at every place $v$ and $\deg D = 0$, where a place is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring. Let $D$ be a divisor, i.e. a finitely supported function from places to $\mathbb{Z}$. On the one side, take `adeleSpace K F`, the supremum over all divisors $E$ of the $K$-submodules $\mathbb{A}(E) = \{\alpha : \prod_v F \mid \forall v,\ v(\alpha_v) \le q_v^{E(v)}\}$ of the full product over places, and inside it the submodule `adeleBddPrincipal K F D`, the join of the preimages of $\mathbb{A}(D)$ and of the image of the diagonal map $F \to \prod_v F$. On the other side, take $H^1(D)$, the quotient of the $F$-subalgebra `repartitions K F` of $\prod_v F$ generated by the families with $v(\alpha_v) \le 1$ for all but finitely many $v$ by the join of the submodule of repartitions satisfying $v(\alpha_v) \le q_v^{D(v)}$ for all $v$ and the submodule of constant repartitions coming from $F$. The assertion is that there exists a $K$-linear isomorphism $e$ from `adeleSpace K F` modulo `adeleBddPrincipal K F D` onto $H^1(D)$ which, for every $a$ in the adèle space and every witness that its underlying family lies in `repartitions K F`, sends the class of $a$ to the class of that family.
--
--   This identifies the two adelic models of $H^1(D)$ used for curves — the index quotient $\mathbb{A}_F/(\mathbb{A}(D)+F)$, in which the index of speciality and Weil differentials are formulated, and the répartition quotient — not merely as abstractly isomorphic $K$-spaces but by the map induced by the identity on families, an adèle being a répartition. It is used in the finiteness statement for $H^1(D)$ together with the duality between $H^1(D)$ and the space of Weil differentials.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_linearEquiv_adeleSpaceQuot_H1.lean

import Mathlib
